cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TACET or cite Crovia's silence proofs, please cite this repository."
title: "TACET: Verifiable Silence for AI Training Disclosure"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Crovia Trust"
    email: info@croviatrust.com
    website: https://croviatrust.com
repository-code: https://github.com/croviatrust/countersign
url: https://croviatrust.com/registry/tacet/
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-19
keywords:
  - AI transparency
  - training data disclosure
  - EU AI Act Article 53
  - transparency log
  - sparse Merkle tree
  - proof of absence
  - OpenTimestamps
  - drand
  - Ed25519
abstract: >
  TACET is a transparency-log protocol whose product is a portable, offline-verifiable
  proof that no training-data disclosure was found on an AI model's public surfaces across
  a range of hourly epochs, each opened by a drand randomness round and closed by a Bitcoin
  block. Verdicts come from a public, versioned predicate over the fetched bytes; every
  observation is signed; silence is the sum of anchored, observed epochs and never accrues
  without observation. Proofs are delivered as unmodified crovia.seal.v1 objects.
references:
  - type: standard
    title: "The Crovia Seal (draft-crovia-seal)"
    url: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-crovia-seal/
    authors:
      - name: "Crovia Trust"
